Z||000000||Ronnie||09-12-2001||06:33 PM||||Someone tel me if the harmonic balancer on an 88 3800 engine is 2 piece or not. Got a friend that has one in a Bonneville and you can actually move the pulleys about a half round with your hand while engine is not started, and hits a dead stop. Making a heavy metal knocking noise while running.Like it has about a halfround of sloppy loose play. Is this a common problem with these engines?||||reg||6
Z||000001||terryk||09-12-2001||09:03 PM||||Replace it ASAP. Yes, it's common but only will lots of miles. You should not me able to move the pulley ring on the center rubber hub. Nothing should move.<P>Makes tons of racket don't it?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000002||Ronnie||09-12-2001||09:48 PM||||Most noise I've heard coming from a pulley of any kind, lol. Thanks, it belongs to a gf of ours . Told her that thing was about ready to let go. How much trouble would it be to replace and how much you think it would cost?||||reg||6
Z||000003||terryk||09-13-2001||12:22 PM||||When the 'ole rubber seperates, it makes an incredibly loud banging noise. Do it soon since it has the potential to damage the crank sensor too.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
